<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Djibo Bakary</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1922">1922</a>–<a href="/years/1998">1998</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Djibo Bakary was a Nigerien trade unionist and politician who led the Sawaba party. As head of the territorial government of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/niger-river">Niger</a> from 1957, he campaigned for a 'no' vote in the 1958 referendum on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-community">French Community</a>, seeking immediate independence. After the 'yes' vote won with French support, his party was banned in 1959 and he went into exile, from where he backed an armed insurgency against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hamani-diori">Hamani Diori</a>.</p></div>
